## Lore

The spaceways equivalent of the bounty hunter, pursuing wanted criminals across
the galaxy. It is dangerous work and a distrusted profession. Local police do
not trust tracers and read them as greedy, reckless mercenaries or vigilantes.

Most adventurers want little to do with these manhunters, because they are known
to turn on former comrades if the price is right - which the book is careful to
say is only true of anarchist and evil characters. The upshot is that galactic
tracers work well with each other, and with the occasional team of adventurers
or mercenaries willing to overlook it.

## GM Notes

Available as a player character.

**At least two of the seven related skill picks must come from Espionage.** The
app offers all seven freely; hold the player to it.

The GM may let a tracer own **a small spaceship** with room for two to eight
passengers and a little cargo. The catalog has no shape for a vessel, so it is
not on the sheet.

Rogue skills are printed at **+6%** - not +5, not +10. It is on the page twice
and it is transcribed as printed.

A tracer may have up to 1D4 cybernetic implants, which there is no field for.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'galactic-tracer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'galactic-tracer';

